   "citations": true
  },
  "sources": 10,
  "docs": 2,
  "seconds": 5.8,
  "answer": "BERT was pre-trained on several corpora. The first corpus is BOOKCORPUS (Zhu et al., 2015) plus English WIKIPEDIA, which is the original data used to train BERT and amounts to 16GB of uncompressed text [1]. The second corpus is CC-NEWS, collected from the English portion of the CommonCrawl News dataset crawled between September 2016 and February 2019, containing 63 million English news articles after filtering, totaling 76GB [1]. The third corpus is OPENWEBTEXT, an open-source recreation of the WebText corpus described in Radford et al. (2019), consisting of web content extracted from URLs shared on Reddit with at least three upvotes, amounting to 38GB [1].",
  "nli": {
   "claims": 0,
   "supported": 0,
   "unverified": 0,
   "contradicted": 0,
   "conflicting": 0
  }
 },
